  "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255908/assets/da921ea4084bc5568d744a1394e6021de70ed9884aadd0fa1a3d9a2f65f5303b.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, stretch it parallel to the $y$-axis by a stretch factor of $4.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$",
